import ../../../ui/source_workspace.dl
import ../../../ui/document_declarations.dl

document editors:
    editor "Studio" containing "😀 f v #" using no UI appearance
    editor "River" containing "😀 f v #" using no UI appearance

to [analyse modifier source] {a pointer to UI source document:document} [using] {a pointer to JSON value:modifiers} [in] {a pointer to UI source workspace:workspace}:
    # A new connection can advertise another modifier order for retained source.
    free UI language client (workspace's client)
    set workspace's client to a UI language client rooted at "file:///workspace"
    set client to workspace's client
    increment document's token epoch
    set work to the next UI language work for client analyzing document at 5.0 seconds
    require condition (work's step = 1) reporting "The modifier fixture did not prepare its project."
    free work's payload
    set response to a new JSON-RPC null
    set work to the UI language reply response at step 1 in client
    free response
    free work's payload
    set legend to a JSON object containing [JSON child "tokenTypes" is (a JSON array containing [a new JSON-RPC text for "function", a new JSON-RPC text for "variable", a new JSON-RPC text for "comment"]), JSON child "tokenModifiers" is (a copy of JSON-RPC node modifiers)]
    set response to a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON number "id" is 2, JSON child "result" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "capabilities" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "semanticTokensProvider" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "legend" is legend])])])]]
    set work to the UI language reply response at step 2 in client
    free response
    free work's payload
    set response to a new JSON-RPC array
    set work to the UI language reply response at step 3 in client
    free response
    free work's payload
    set response to a new JSON-RPC array
    set work to the UI language reply response at step 4 in client
    free response
    free work's payload
    set position to the UI analysis position for source byte 0 in document
    set row to (the JSON number named "line" in position) as an integer
    free position
    set tokens to a JSON array containing [
        a new JSON-RPC integer for row, a new JSON-RPC integer for 3, a new JSON-RPC integer for 1, a new JSON-RPC integer for 0, a new JSON-RPC integer for 3,
        a new JSON-RPC integer for 0, a new JSON-RPC integer for 2, a new JSON-RPC integer for 1, a new JSON-RPC integer for 1, a new JSON-RPC integer for 1,
        a new JSON-RPC integer for 0, a new JSON-RPC integer for 2, a new JSON-RPC integer for 1, a new JSON-RPC integer for 2, a new JSON-RPC integer for 2
    ]
    set response to a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON number "id" is 6, JSON child "result" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "data" is tokens])]]
    set work to the UI language reply response at step 6 in client
    free response
    require condition (work's step = 0) reporting "The modifier fixture did not finish its analysis."

set instance to an instance of editors
set window to the address of instance
set workspace to a UI source workspace in window rooted at "file:///workspace"
set studio to the UI source editor labeled "Studio" in workspace
set river to the UI source editor labeled "River" in workspace
set files to a new JSON-RPC object
configure UI source document (river's document) named "river.dl" at "file:///workspace/river.dl" prefixed by "import vocabulary.dl\n\n" using UI CPU analysis with files files
free files
set modifiers to a JSON array containing [a new JSON-RPC text for "constant", a new JSON-RPC text for "nested"]
analyse modifier source (studio's document) using modifiers in workspace
analyse modifier source (river's document) using modifiers in workspace
set theme to [
    @intrinsic("construct", UI source token style, "function", UI ink 10 0 0),
    @intrinsic("construct", UI source token style, "variable", UI ink 55 0 0),
    @intrinsic("construct", UI source token style, "comment", UI ink 50 0 0),
    @intrinsic("construct", UI source token style, "function.nested", UI ink 20 0 0),
    @intrinsic("construct", UI source token style, "*.constant", UI ink 30 0 0),
    @intrinsic("construct", UI source token style, "function.constant.nested", UI ink 40 0 0)
]
present UI source workspace workspace using theme
set editor to workspace's editors
loop while editor != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI source editor):
    set color to (the UI value for (editor's node) in window)'s colors
    require condition ((color's start = 5) and (color's ink's red = 40)) reporting "A source ignored its most specific semantic modifiers or Unicode prefix."
    require condition (color's next's ink's red = 30) reporting "A wildcard modifier style did not apply to another token type."
    require condition (color's next's next's ink's red = 50) reporting "A modifier style applied to the wrong token type."
    set editor to editor's next
set revision to instance's revision
present UI source workspace workspace using theme
require condition (instance's revision = revision) reporting "Unchanged modifier styles repainted an unchanged editor."
set generation to studio's document's token generation
analyse modifier source (studio's document) using modifiers in workspace
require condition (studio's document's token generation = generation) reporting "An identical semantic legend invalidated retained colors."
set revision to instance's revision
present UI source workspace workspace using theme
require condition (instance's revision = revision) reporting "An identical semantic refresh repainted retained colors."
free modifiers
set modifiers to a JSON array containing [a new JSON-RPC text for "nested", a new JSON-RPC text for "constant"]
analyse modifier source (studio's document) using modifiers in workspace
require condition (studio's document's token generation > generation) reporting "Changing only the modifier legend retained obsolete colors."
present UI source workspace workspace using theme
set color to (the UI value for (studio's node) in window)'s colors
require condition ((color's next's ink's red = 55) and (color's next's next's ink's red = 30)) reporting "Modifier bits did not follow the current language legend."
set color to (the UI value for (river's node) in window)'s colors
require condition (color's next's ink's red = 30) reporting "One project's modifier legend replaced another project's retained legend."
set tie to [
    @intrinsic("construct", UI source token style, "function.constant", UI ink 60 0 0),
    @intrinsic("construct", UI source token style, "*.constant", UI ink 70 0 0),
    @intrinsic("construct", UI source token style, "function.constant", UI ink 80 0 0)
]
set selected to the UI source token style index for "function" with modifiers 2 from modifiers using tie
require condition (selected = 2) reporting "Exact types and final equally specific rules did not win their style ties."
set selected to the UI source token style index for "function" with modifiers 1 from modifiers using tie
require condition (selected = -1) reporting "A style matched a modifier absent from the token."
free modifiers
set modifiers to a new JSON-RPC array
set index to 0
loop while index < 31:
    add (a new JSON-RPC text for ("flag" + (the string form of index))) to the JSON array modifiers
    increment index
set high to [@intrinsic("construct", UI source token style, "function.flag30", UI ink 90 0 0)]
set selected to the UI source token style index for "function" with modifiers 1073741824 from modifiers using high
require condition (selected = 0) reporting "The highest protocol modifier bit overflowed its style lookup."
free modifiers
free UI source workspace workspace
close window
print line "Studio and River share semantic modifier styles, Unicode mapping, legend ownership and color caching."
